From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan Hertenberger <erde74@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:02:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 08/26] plan9: zero-length reads and writes with a valid buffer
 (the kernel checks 0x1); rustc's file locks without locking (as cargo's);
 jobserver from 9front-rust

9front's kernel validates a buffer's address at zero bytes too: an empty
slice's dangling pointer killed cargo's child before exec (an empty
environment value). std gives such calls a byte of its own (buf_ptr).
rustc's incremental sessions take their lock without one on plan9 (no
advisory locks), as cargo does there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
